# During the design effort only docs/ merges to main, and prototypes are
# scratch-only and never merge (AGENTS.md, issue #1). So this file denies the
# repository root by default and allows back what belongs there.
#
# The reason it is an allowlist and not a list of binary patterns: a Go test
# binary is named after its module and carries no extension, so `ferryproto5`
# matches no pattern anyone would think to write. A 4.3 MB one reached main in
# PR #24 and had to be purged by history rewrite.
#
# Widened for #15, which needs a Windows runner and therefore needs .github/
# committed. The deny-by-default is NOT weakened: this is one more entry in the
# allowlist, and every pattern below still applies inside it.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/docs/
!/.github/

# Belt and braces, for anyone working in a subdirectory or on a proto branch.
/proto/
*.test
*.out
*.exe
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.prof
